---
title: Custom fields, batch, and export
date: '2026-06-16'
tags:
  - added
summary: Custom field definitions, confidence-based review flags, batch upload, re-process, and JSON/CSV/XLSX export in the source app.
---

The source app added **custom field definitions**, **validation** and
**confidence-based review flags** for extracted values. It also added batch
upload, a re-process action, document delete, and export to CSV, JSON and Excel.
Provider selection was abstracted in the extraction layer.

The accompanying marketing page described early access, but its form only
sent an application when a separate endpoint was configured. No connected
public signup or hosted extraction is established by this release. The former
landing screenshot was withdrawn here because it displayed unverified speed,
pricing and access claims. Matched light/dark captures of the actual app,
with narrated films and captions, remain a release-media task.

## Current evaluation note · 2026-09-25

This June source update is not a hosted processing release. Evaluating the app
requires repository access, Supabase Auth/database/private Storage with the
app's migrations, a model provider key, and a long-lived process for the current
background pipeline. No public Docpeel processing origin, completed provider
run, or speed benchmark has been verified for this entry. The separate static
landing's illustrated invoice is synthetic design, not a product capture.
Matched light/dark screenshots and films will be linked only after an actual
synthetic-document run, visual review, and public byte/hash verification.
